.TH SYSCONF 3 "September 20, 2026"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
sysconf \- return a DiscoBSD runtime limit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B long sysconf(int name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sysconf
returns the value of a runtime limit selected by
.IR name .
DiscoBSD exposes only limits backed by a fixed kernel or libc contract:
.TP
.B _SC_ARG_MAX
The maximum combined argument and environment size, 5120 bytes.
.TP
.B _SC_CLK_TCK
The 60 ticks per second returned by
.IR times (3).
.TP
.B _SC_NGROUPS_MAX
The 16 group slots in a process credential.
.TP
.B _SC_OPEN_MAX
The 30 descriptor slots in a process file table.
.TP
.B _SC_JOB_CONTROL
One, because the kernel implements job control.
.PP
An unsupported selector returns -1 and sets
.I errno
to
.BR EINVAL .
.SH SEE ALSO
times(3), unistd(5)
